[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3581797340","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/3338#issuecomment-3581797340","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/3338","id":3581797340,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7VfePc","user":{"login":"atomiks","id":22450188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDUwMTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22450188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks","html_url":"https://github.com/atomiks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-26T15:18:11Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T15:18:11Z","body":"This change was added here for context: https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/2473","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3581797340/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3582889506","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/3338#issuecomment-3582889506","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/3338","id":3582889506,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7Vjo4i","user":{"login":"Domcsore","id":2321197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMjExOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2321197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore","html_url":"https://github.com/Domcsore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-26T19:24:03Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T19:24:03Z","body":"To clarify, the fact the value is missing from the `FormData` is not the issue as this behavior is expected, the specific issue I'm facing is auto focusing invalid fields. \n\nWhen submitting a form and a field is invalid, the external library focuses the first invalid field with 'x' name. With other components in Base UI I can simply grab a ref to the underlying input and 'pass on' the focus to the trigger but with RadioGroup, this is impossible because no input with the name exists.\n\nThis behavior should and does work with native radio inputs so I feel it should be replicated here.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3582889506/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3583036148","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/3338#issuecomment-3583036148","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/3338","id":3583036148,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7VkMr0","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-26T20:05:39Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T20:05:39Z","body":"> When submitting a form and a field is invalid, the external library focuses the first invalid field with 'x' name\n\nWhat library are you integrating with? Would be great if you could share a sandbox 🙏","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3583036148/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3588911608","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/3338#issuecomment-3588911608","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/3338","id":3588911608,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7V6nH4","user":{"login":"Domcsore","id":2321197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMjExOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2321197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore","html_url":"https://github.com/Domcsore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Domcsore/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-28T11:10:29Z","updated_at":"2025-11-30T03:50:36Z","body":"> What library are you integrating with? Would be great if you could share a sandbox 🙏\n\n@mj12albert Sure, it's Conform - here's the sandbox: https://codesandbox.io/p/devbox/base-ui-radio-demonstration-mwjkl3\n\nIf no values are entered on any of the inputs (essentially making them all invalid) and submit is hit - the first field to be highlighted is the select component. The first invalid input in the form, the radio in this case, should be highlighted but as the underlying input has no name it never gets focused.\n\nWith native, all the individual radio inputs have a name. As so, the first radio button would get focus.\n\nI believe [2473](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/2473) fixes one native issue but introduces another. If this is deemed an issue, one possible fix could be to add `name`s to the hidden, individual, radio inputs.\n\nEdit: Removed disabled suggestion as this prevents focus and would not solve the issue.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3588911608/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3612584525","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/3338#issuecomment-3612584525","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/3338","id":3612584525,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7XU6pN","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-04T14:41:55Z","updated_at":"2025-12-04T14:57:44Z","body":"@Domcsore I got it to work following their [Radix example](https://github.com/edmundhung/conform/tree/main/examples/radix-ui), which requires `useControl` from `@conform-to/react/future`: https://codesandbox.io/p/devbox/hardcore-colden-mf2c6m\n\nYou need to make your own hidden input and register it to `useControl`, then move the focus to the radio group:\n```tsx\nconst radioInputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);\nconst radioControl = useControl({\n  onFocus() {\n    radioInputRef.current?.focus();\n  },\n}); \n\n<input ref={radioControl.register} name={fields.testRadio.name} hidden />\n<RadioGroup\n  value={radioControl.value ?? \"\"}\n  onValueChange={(value) => radioControl.change(value as string)}\n  inputRef={radioInputRef}\n/>\n```\n\nConform uses [`formElement.elements`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLFormElement/elements) to find the first error to focus so it's kind of strict (e.g. compared to RHF): https://github.com/edmundhung/conform/blob/fe389a8a3f6d7d0663b41a23fa51be9e14443c09/packages/conform-react/future/dom.ts#L211-L227\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3612584525/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]]